  "describe": "A row of three stacked pairs, Gate B34, Seat 14C (centred) and Boards 09:40 (blue, at the end), with small muted labels over 28 dp values; then Terminal 2E, Hall L (small), Flight … AF 1234 across the width, Status Delayed 25 min in red and Bag drop closes 08:55 at the end. The accessibility tree has exactly one node per pair: \"Gate, B34\", \"Seat, 14 C\", \"Boards, 09:40\", \"Terminal, 2E, Hall L\", \"Flight, AF 1234\", \"Status, Delayed 25 min\", \"Bag drop closes, 08:55\". At 220 dp the large values shrink to fit their thirds; at 480 dp the pairs follow the width.",
